Step 3: Run the Automation via Docker

Running ZAP inside a Docker container ensures your automation is portable, easily repeatable, and doesn't require local GUI installations.
Run the following command to execute your configuration file:
bash
docker run -v $(pwd):/workspace -t ghcr.io/zaproxy/zaproxy:stable zap.sh -cmd -autorun /workspace/zap.yaml

Note: If you run into API authorization errors during localized container setups, you can temporarily bypass them using the -config api.disablekey=true flag.

Step 4: Integrate into your CI/CD Pipeline

To achieve continuous security testing, embed this execution layer directly into your automated build workflows.

GitHub Actions Example

yaml
name: OWASP Security Scan
on: [push]

jobs:
  zap_scan:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    name: Scan the web application
    steps:
      - name: Checkout Code
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: ZAP Scan
        uses: zaproxy/action-baseline@v0.13.0
        with:
          target: 'https://your-staging-app.com'
          rules_file_name: '.zaprules'
          fail_action: true # Fails the build if high-risk bugs are found


Jenkins Pipeline Example

groovy
stage('OWASP ZAP Security Scan') {
    steps {
        script {
            sh 'docker run -v $(pwd):/zap/wrk:rw -t ghcr.io/zaproxy/zaproxy:stable zap-baseline.py -t https://your-staging-app.com -r owasp_report.html'
        }
    }
}


Step 5: Handle Authentication (For Deep Scans)

A basic automated scan only crawls public-facing pages. To test for deep vulnerabilities (like Broken Access Control or SQL Injection behind a login wall), you must automate authentication:
1. Proxy Method: Run your functional end-to-end tests (e.g., using Selenium or Playwright) and route their network traffic through ZAP acting as a local proxy. ZAP will automatically capture the active session tokens and run its security scans against those authenticated pages.
2. Script Method: Provide a script or a target Header inside your ZAP Automation configuration containing a valid JWT or Bearer token generated right before the scan phase starts.
